WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.190 --> 00:00:01.690
- I'm back and hanging with the cast

00:00:01.690 --> 00:00:04.220
and creators of "Happiest Season" on Hulu.

00:00:04.220 --> 00:00:06.869
So we've got Kristen
Stewart, Mackenzie Davis,

00:00:06.869 --> 00:00:08.360
(audience clapping)
and Mary Steenburgen on Skype,

00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:11.526
and Mary Holland and Clea DuVall
here in the studio with us.

00:00:11.526 --> 00:00:13.907
Movie casts can get pretty close,

00:00:13.907 --> 00:00:17.130
but how well do the ladies
of "Happiest Season"

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:18.550
really know each other?

00:00:18.550 --> 00:00:19.840
It's time to find out with something,

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:21.530
straight out of our high school yearbooks

00:00:21.530 --> 00:00:23.674
called "Who's Most Likely".

00:00:23.674 --> 00:00:27.716
♪ Who's most likely ♪
(audience clapping)

00:00:27.716 --> 00:00:28.898
(Kelly laughing)

00:00:28.898 --> 00:00:31.565
- Jesse, that was a good jingle!

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:34.160
Alright, it's pretty simple ladies.

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:37.020
I will ask you, who's most
likely to do something

00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:39.590
and you all get to vote
on who that would be.

00:00:39.590 --> 00:00:41.020
So first, Mary Holland.

00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:43.770
Who's most likely to be the party girl?

00:00:43.770 --> 00:00:45.860
- I mean, it's gotta be Mary Steenburgen.

00:00:45.860 --> 00:00:47.370
- [Host] Are you serious?
- Hands down, oh yeah.

00:00:47.370 --> 00:00:48.430
Mary would host...

00:00:48.430 --> 00:00:49.800
- Are you serious, Isabel?

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:51.130
- Oh yeah, yeah.

00:00:51.130 --> 00:00:52.567
She is a party animal.

00:00:52.567 --> 00:00:55.604
- And Kelly, Kelly, one of these days,

00:00:55.604 --> 00:00:58.140
you're gonna be there.

00:00:58.140 --> 00:00:58.973
- [Holland] Yes.

00:00:58.973 --> 00:00:59.867
- I wanna be there!

00:00:59.867 --> 00:01:00.790
And I want pie to be there.

00:01:00.790 --> 00:01:02.240
- [Mary] Yeah, yeah.

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:03.340
- That's amazing.

00:01:03.340 --> 00:01:04.560
I love that answer.

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:06.480
Wait, what are you talking about?

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:07.711
- She would host
(Kelly laughing)

00:01:07.711 --> 00:01:09.080
these incredible game night parties.

00:01:09.080 --> 00:01:10.290
I remember there was one.

00:01:10.290 --> 00:01:12.042
She had us all over at her apartment,

00:01:12.042 --> 00:01:13.890
that she and Ted were staying in

00:01:13.890 --> 00:01:17.230
and we played running charades
and it got very intense.

00:01:17.230 --> 00:01:18.860
It got very competitive.
(laughs)

00:01:18.860 --> 00:01:20.870
And yeah, we had the most fun.

00:01:20.870 --> 00:01:21.960
But Mary loves games.

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:23.900
- Yeah, I wanna be
invited to a game night.

00:01:23.900 --> 00:01:24.733
I'm just saying.

00:01:24.733 --> 00:01:25.930
I'm just inviting myself.

00:01:25.930 --> 00:01:26.763
Um and I love

00:01:26.763 --> 00:01:27.596
- [Steenburgen] Oh you will be.

00:01:27.596 --> 00:01:29.710
- That I did not know you were
gonna be the answer to that.

00:01:29.710 --> 00:01:30.543
That's amazing.

00:01:30.543 --> 00:01:31.376
All right,

00:01:31.376 --> 00:01:32.209
next one's for Clea.

00:01:32.209 --> 00:01:34.770
- So who's most likely to solve a puzzle?

00:01:34.770 --> 00:01:37.919
- Okay, well, I know that it's not really

00:01:37.919 --> 00:01:39.796
Um, it's not really, uh...

00:01:39.796 --> 00:01:43.790
You're not supposed to do this,
but I would say maybe, me.

00:01:43.790 --> 00:01:44.623
- [Kelly] Oh!

00:01:44.623 --> 00:01:45.500
- [Clea] Or Mackenzie or

00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:47.160
- Mackenzie!
- Mary also.

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:48.476
- Oh, somebody just said Mackenzie

00:01:48.476 --> 00:01:49.625
(Kelly laughs)

00:01:49.625 --> 00:01:52.328
- (indistinct) doing a crossword...

00:01:52.328 --> 00:01:53.630
- We did crosswords.

00:01:53.630 --> 00:01:55.810
We also did a lot of escape rooms.

00:01:55.810 --> 00:01:56.643
- [Kelly] Oh my gosh!

00:01:56.643 --> 00:01:57.950
I love escape rooms.

00:01:57.950 --> 00:01:58.783
- [Clea] You do?

00:01:58.783 --> 00:02:00.330
- I have done so many, My band,

00:02:00.330 --> 00:02:01.410
We love them.

00:02:01.410 --> 00:02:02.561
- We are obsessed.

00:02:02.561 --> 00:02:03.394
- [Holland] Obsessed.

00:02:03.394 --> 00:02:04.880
- [Kelly] They are so fun.
- And we did every escape room

00:02:04.880 --> 00:02:06.541
I think that Pittsburgh had to offer.

00:02:06.541 --> 00:02:08.295
(Kelly laughing)
(audience laughing)

00:02:08.295 --> 00:02:10.320
- [Clea] It was so much fun, um yeah.

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:11.170
- Are you good at them?

00:02:11.170 --> 00:02:13.360
Who's the best at an
escape room in this group?

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:14.673
- I mean, this is gonna contemptuous.

00:02:14.673 --> 00:02:16.710
- We all bring our own strengths.

00:02:16.710 --> 00:02:18.510
I think we can say everybody

00:02:18.510 --> 00:02:19.380
brings something different to this.

00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:20.523
- Except for me.

00:02:20.523 --> 00:02:21.913
- That is not true, Mary.
- I would still be in there,

00:02:21.913 --> 00:02:23.176
in Pittsburgh.
- You did so well

00:02:23.176 --> 00:02:24.962
when we did escape room.

00:02:24.962 --> 00:02:27.010
And am not just being nice.

00:02:27.010 --> 00:02:27.843
- It's such a lie.

00:02:27.843 --> 00:02:28.676
- It's such a...

00:02:28.676 --> 00:02:30.100
(Kelly laughs)
(guests laughing)

00:02:30.100 --> 00:02:32.330
- [Clea] We can offline about
this, but you did great.

00:02:32.330 --> 00:02:33.550
You did, you did.

00:02:33.550 --> 00:02:35.780
- Wait, there's not one of
you that, like stood out,

00:02:35.780 --> 00:02:37.060
Cause I'm gonna tell
you right now, if you...

00:02:37.060 --> 00:02:38.700
- [Clea] MacKenzie is trying
to give the correct answer

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:39.533
and no one would let her.

00:02:39.533 --> 00:02:40.366
- [Mary] MacKenzie!

00:02:40.366 --> 00:02:41.199
- [Kelly] Oh!

00:02:41.199 --> 00:02:42.110
- The correct answer is, it's Clea.

00:02:42.110 --> 00:02:42.953
- [Clea] Yeah.

00:02:42.953 --> 00:02:43.861
- [Mary] It's Clea absolutely.

00:02:43.861 --> 00:02:45.670
(Kelly laughing)
(audience laughing)

00:02:45.670 --> 00:02:47.661
- Clea was like, she wants to say it.

00:02:47.661 --> 00:02:48.550
(Clea laughing)
(guests laughing)

00:02:48.550 --> 00:02:49.720
This one is for Kristen,

00:02:49.720 --> 00:02:52.783
so who's most likely to
distract everyone on set?

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:58.236
- Uh, Mary, probably.
- [Kelly] Which Mary?

00:02:58.236 --> 00:03:00.263
- Oh, uh Steenburgen.

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:02.940
- [Kelly] What! Are you partying so much,

00:03:02.940 --> 00:03:04.325
nobody can get anything done?

00:03:04.325 --> 00:03:05.621
(guests laughing)

00:03:05.621 --> 00:03:07.040
- No, all of us could
focus when Mary was around.

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:08.893
- [Mary] I have a hard time behaving.

00:03:08.893 --> 00:03:10.718
- [Kelly] Oh my God, I love you.

00:03:10.718 --> 00:03:13.163
- I've done this job too long.

00:03:13.163 --> 00:03:14.120
(Kelly laughing)

00:03:14.120 --> 00:03:15.750
- I think it's the Southern roots.

00:03:15.750 --> 00:03:16.670
That's what it is,

00:03:16.670 --> 00:03:18.540
cause I like to have a good time too.

00:03:18.540 --> 00:03:19.580
And that's amazing.

00:03:19.580 --> 00:03:20.413
I love...

00:03:20.413 --> 00:03:21.246
Okay.

00:03:21.246 --> 00:03:22.950
And one more, let's go to MacKenzie.

00:03:22.950 --> 00:03:25.395
So who's most likely to
drink and play games?

00:03:25.395 --> 00:03:27.313
You're gonna say Mary aren't you?

00:03:27.313 --> 00:03:29.805
(Kelly laughs)
(guests laugh)

00:03:29.805 --> 00:03:32.300
- Well ,maybe, I would say most likely

00:03:32.300 --> 00:03:33.261
to drink and play games,

00:03:33.261 --> 00:03:36.153
I feel like Kristen and I.

00:03:36.153 --> 00:03:37.070
- [Steenburgen] I think,

00:03:37.070 --> 00:03:38.422
Yeah, you and Kristen.

00:03:38.422 --> 00:03:39.255
- (indistinct) honestly,

00:03:39.255 --> 00:03:42.700
everyone actually liked to
hang out with each other

00:03:42.700 --> 00:03:43.533
on this movie.

00:03:43.533 --> 00:03:44.366
It was fun on set,

00:03:44.366 --> 00:03:46.040
but me and MacKenzie were talking about

00:03:46.040 --> 00:03:46.873
how surprised we were

00:03:46.873 --> 00:03:49.578
at everyone's willingness
to engage all the time.

00:03:49.578 --> 00:03:51.852
It was very fun to have so many friends.

00:03:51.852 --> 00:03:52.700
- [MacKenzie] Yeah.
- [Steenburgen] Yeah.

00:03:52.700 --> 00:03:54.300
- We were like feeling so popular.

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:56.060
Cause we had each other for so long.

00:03:56.060 --> 00:03:56.893
I was like,

00:03:56.893 --> 00:03:57.910
wow! I have like 10 friends right now.

00:03:57.910 --> 00:03:58.840
- Yeah. That's awesome.

00:03:58.840 --> 00:04:00.777
I love that y'all had such a good time

00:04:00.777 --> 00:04:01.682
and maybe, not you Clea,

00:04:01.682 --> 00:04:03.330
you're probably like shut up!

00:04:03.330 --> 00:04:04.620
- [Clea] No.
(Kelly laughing)

00:04:04.620 --> 00:04:05.700
I had a great time.

00:04:05.700 --> 00:04:07.250
I loved all of them so much.

00:04:07.250 --> 00:04:08.159
And I...

00:04:08.159 --> 00:04:10.410
you know, I really wanted to
play with them and I couldn't.

00:04:10.410 --> 00:04:12.111
So sometimes I felt like, you know,

00:04:12.111 --> 00:04:13.620
like the kid on the outside be like,

00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:14.970
are they playing the game?

00:04:14.970 --> 00:04:16.030
Oh, they're playing the game.
- [Kelly] By the way

00:04:16.030 --> 00:04:17.718
- And I have to stay here.
I'll set up the shot.

00:04:17.718 --> 00:04:19.610
Yeah, I'll set up the shot.

00:04:19.610 --> 00:04:21.590
- That's, by the way
that is the exact feeling

00:04:21.590 --> 00:04:23.062
of like me touring with
my band for 20 years.

00:04:23.062 --> 00:04:24.410
And everybody's like,

00:04:24.410 --> 00:04:26.770
Oh my God! So we saw this,
this, this, and like,

00:04:26.770 --> 00:04:28.380
I was doing like 17 interviews.

00:04:28.380 --> 00:04:29.213
And I was like,

00:04:29.213 --> 00:04:30.497
so glad you had such a good time.

00:04:30.497 --> 00:04:31.598
- [Holland] Yeah
(laughs)

00:04:31.598 --> 00:04:33.370
(guests laughing)
- It's like, cool.

00:04:33.370 --> 00:04:34.203
I'm glad.

00:04:34.203 --> 00:04:35.490
So it's so fun for you.

00:04:35.490 --> 00:04:36.670
I got to talk about myself

00:04:36.670 --> 00:04:37.596
for like 11 hours straight,

00:04:37.596 --> 00:04:39.813
but anyway, um, we'll edit that out,

00:04:39.813 --> 00:04:41.185
So I don't seem so angry.

00:04:41.185 --> 00:04:43.395
(guests laughing)

00:04:43.395 --> 00:04:44.304
- No keep it,

00:04:44.304 --> 00:04:45.137
keep it!

00:04:45.137 --> 00:04:46.713
- I don't know, maybe
everyone's feeling it.

00:04:46.713 --> 00:04:49.760
Thank you so much to all
of you for being here.

00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:51.382
Y'all be sure to watch "Happiest Season".

00:04:51.382 --> 00:04:52.215
(audience clapping)

00:04:52.215 --> 00:04:54.070
It's starting November 25th on Hulu.

00:04:54.070 --> 00:04:54.903
If you wanna laugh,

00:04:54.903 --> 00:04:56.053
you gotta watch.

